  "notes": "Ajiri (Eloyi) orthography uses West African conventions including ɛ, ɔ, and ŋ. Multigraphs like gb, kp, sh, zh, and prenasalized/labialized/palatalized consonants (mb, nz, kw, gw, gy, ngb, ngy) are treated as single tokens. The retroflex click letter ǃ appears rarely in the frequency list, possibly as punctuation or a borrowed phoneme.",
